ref: apachecon-eu-2000

The following organizations exhibited at ApacheCon Europe 2000.

*For information on
exhibit and sponsorship opportunities, please contact Jeffrey Wainhause at
<>*

### Exhibit Hours

The exhibit floor is open
during the following hours:

- Tuesday, 24 October 2000: 11h45 until 21h00

- Wednesday, 25 October 2000: 11h45 until 18h00

## ApacheCon Europe 2000 Exhibitors

### Apache Software Foundation

Booth 2

The Apache Software Foundation is the unifying organisation behind
the various Apache projects, such as the Web server, the XML parser,
the Java servlet engine, and others. Come stop by our booth to find
out more. Bring some business cards and we'll make you some baggage
tags!

![[]Apache Week](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/aw_white_135x38.gif)

### [[]Apache Week](http://www.apacheweek.com/)

Booth 14

Published weekly on the web and distributed via email to over
10,000 people world-wide, C2Net's
Apache Week is the definitive online resource for all users of
Apache and Apache-based web servers. Apache Week
covers in-depth features and provides simple tutorials and
how-to's for novice and expert users alike.

![[]Berkeley Software Design Inc. (BSDi)](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/bsdilogo_135x59.gif)

### [[]Berkeley Software Design Inc. (BSDi)](https://web.archive.org/web/20001019041459/http://www.bsd.com:80/)

**Conference Proceedings Co-sponsor**

Booth 72

Berkeley Software Design Inc. (BSDi) develops Internet
Infrastructure grade hardware and software solutions for systems, networks,
appliances, and users. Our software solutions include the commercial
BSD/OS, and the open source FreeBSD, and our hardware includes a wide
range of 1U, 2U, and larger rack mount IA32 architecture servers.
Please visit http://www.bsd.com/ for more information.

![[]Covalent Technologies](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/covalent_135x50.gif)

### [[]Covalent Technologies](https://web.archive.org/web/20001019062337/http://www.covalent.net:80/)

**Expo Welcoming Reception**

**Coffee Mug**

Booth 94

Covalent Technologies is the leader in e-commerce solutions and
secured data applications for the Apache Web server platform. Covalent
develops commercial software enhancements for Apache, including
several plug in security and management modules, and is the only source
for comprehensive commercial support for the Apache Web server
platform.

![[]Eliad Technologies, Inc.](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/eliad_69x50.gif)

### [[]Eliad Technologies, Inc.](http://www.eliad.com/)

Booth 100

Eliad Technologies, Inc. provides Java™ technology-based
development solutions for optimal data visualization in tables, grids,
and spreadsheets. Discover the JSmartGrid™ 1.0, the smallest
Swing grid component (162 KB) specifically designed for the
Java™ 2 Platform v1.3.0. The JSmartGrid™ extensive API with its
scalable presentation abilities simplifies design for Web, database
and B2B applications. It gives developers more flexibility in
displaying all types of data, including XML documents.

![[]IBM](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/IBM_96x39.jpg)

### [[]IBM](http://www.ibm.com/)

**Social Event**

Booth 112

At IBM, we strive to lead in the creation, development and
manufacture of the industry's most advanced information technologies. IBM
has an application framework and provides an application server and
web design tools that give you the performance and flexibility you
want, to build the kind of web sites your companies and customers need.
IBM offers partnership programs that provide support and training
to help you get going - and growing - fast. IBM is e-business.

![[]internet.com](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/apache-today_135x49.gif)

### [[]internet.com](http://internet.com/)

Booth 20

INTERESTED IN THE LATEST INFORMATION ON APACHE? Then visit
apachetoday.com for your daily source of Apache News and Information.
Including discussion forums, editorials, newsletters and more. Part of the
internet.com network of sites - <[[]http://apachetoday.com/](http://apachetoday.com/)>.

![[]MyComponents](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/mycomponents_135x35.gif)

### [[]MyComponents](https://web.archive.org/web/20001018075918/http://www.mycomponents.com:80/)

Booth 4

MyComponents is a global brokerage hub for reusable Web based
applications. Established in May 2000, our mission is to empower all kind
of WebMediaries (ISPs- ASPs, …) in developing and maintaining
robust Web applications, enabling them to offer added value to
their customers and to open new revenue streams. The advanced version of
MyComponents.com is scheduled to be launched in Q4 2000.

![[]O'Reilly Network](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/oranet_110x80.jpg)

### [[]O'Reilly Network](http://www.oreillynet.com/)

**Media Pavilion**

Booth 14

The O'Reilly Network is the online source for developers interested
in open and emerging technologies, including new platforms,
programming languages, and operating systems. Just like O'Reilly &
Associates' books, the hub and its affiliate sites provide in-depth
technical information, clearly and consistently, for expert developers.

### [[]OpenBSD](http://www.openbsd.org/)

Booth 28

OpenBSD, the “secure by default” multi-platform OS
derived from 4.4BSD, has a no-compromise full disclosure security stance
backed by a thorough source code audit. Tightly integrated strong
cryptography—including OpenSSH and OpenSSL—further
hardens the OS. Self-financed through CD-ROM sales, OpenBSD is released
under a Berkeley-style license.

![[]StoneSoft](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/stonesoft_120x37.gif)

### [[]StoneSoft](https://web.archive.org/web/20001109075300/http://www.stonebeat.com:80/)

Booth 108

The StoneBeat product family from Stonesoft enables the building of
mission critical systems, Internet services and e-commerce systems
where network downtime is not an option and throughput,
responsiveness and reliability are everything. The StoneBeat product family
includes high availability, load-balancing solutions for Firewalls,
Cache Servers, Web Servers and Content Servers.

![[]Sun Microsystems](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/sunlogo_135x80.gif)

### [[]Sun Microsystems](http://www.sun.com/)

**Internet Pavilion**

Booth 78

Since its inception in 1982, a singular vision - The Network Is The
Computer(tm) - has propelled Sun Microsystems, Inc. to its position
as a leading provider of industrial-strength hardware, software and
services that power the Internet and allow companies worldwide to
".com" their businesses. With $12.4 billion in annual revenues, Sun
can be found in more than 170 countries and at www.sun.com.

![[]Thawte](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/thawte_133x49.gif)

### [[]Thawte](http://www.thawte.com/)

Booth 104

Thawte Consulting is a world leader in PKI technology and SSL
certificates. For the past 4 years Thawte has been providing SSL
certificates to the Apache server community. Their extensive experience and
understanding make them the undisputed leader in SSL certificates
and PKI solutions for Apache servers.

![[]UnixNT News](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/unixnt_133x31.gif)

### [[]UnixNT News](https://web.archive.org/web/20001217181100/http://www.unixntnews.com:80/subs/subscriptions.cgi?code=ApacheCon)

Booth 24

UnixNt news is the leading open user system magazine. Published 10
times a year UnixNT provides insight and analysis into vendor
strategies, the value of product announcements and real life experiences
of IT managers. Month by month the magazine keeps readers abreast of
all the latest technologies, trends, and products. For your free
subscription visit our website at
www.unixntnews.com/subs/subscriptions.cgi?code=ApacheCon
or phone Customer services on 020 7453 5985. For
the printed version you can stop at the .cgi bit and leave off the
?code=

![[]Wrox Press](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/wrox_120x114.gif)

### Wrox Press

Booth 16

One of the leading information providers for the programming
community, Wrox Press is a unique publishing house with an editorial
structure developed to meet the specific needs of the constantly evolving
computer industry. Our authors are all professional programmers
keen to share their knowledge and experience to bring you
authoritative, timely solutions to real-world programming problems. "Programmer
to Programmer" is not just our slogan; it's the way we write our
books.

![[]XML.com](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/xmlcom_120x49.jpg)

### [[]XML.com](https://web.archive.org/web/20001017144847/http://www.xml.com:80/pub)

Booth 14

XML.com is the premier site where the XML community shares
resources, information and solutions. The site is specially designed to
serve developers who are already working with XML, as well as Web
developers who want to understand XML's power and complexity. We cover
controversial issues from the front lines on topics like XSL and EDI.

![[]Xo3](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/xo3_135x37.gif)

### [[]Xo3](https://web.archive.org/web/20001214123000/http://www.xo3.com:80/cgi-bin/bahia09/bahia09.exe?navigate+bythestars+xo3newsite-23+1)

Booth 4

Xo3, the Portal Agency, is specialized in building complex web
architectures and in providing key clients with state of the art
solutions and integrated eBusiness services. It focuses on empowering
Webmediaries to take the best out of the new generation of XML Portal
architectures and helps them offer more added-value to their own
customers. Located in Geneva (Switzerland), Xo3 has been selected various
times has one of the key promising European start-ups.

![[]Zen Computing](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/zen-computing_135x45.jpg)

### [[]Zen Computing](https://web.archive.org/web/20001013001119/http://www.zen.co.za:80/)

Booth 76

Zen Computing is a software company specialising in advanced web
applications that utilise open, extensible industry standards. The
company's core focus is the development of collaborative publishing
technologies. Zen Computing is based in Johannesburg, South Africa.
http://www.zen.co.za/

![[]Zend](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/zend_113x52.gif)

### [[]Zend](http://www.zend.com/)

Booth 106

Zend Technologies Ltd. Is an Israeli startup company,specializing
in Internet infrastructure software. Our mission is to provide
viability and backing for PHP-based Web solutions. At the same time, we
are committed to the advancement of PHP as a widely distributed
open-source scripting language. Zend products have been designed to meet
the requirements of web site and Intranet developers, and of
enterprises and service providers who need to build rich dynamic
applications. Several Zend products aim to increase developers’
productivity, as well as the performance of their sites. Other products
provide mission-critical value, such as protection of proprietary source
codes. In addition to developing and marketing products, Zend
anticipates establishing a strong and dependable technical support
business, in order to lend support to the community of PHP users.

## Invitation to Exhibit at ApacheCon Europe 2000

Exhibition: October 24-25, 2000

Conference: October 23-25, 2000

Olympia Conference Centre

London, England

### Come exhibit and meet 1,000 European Apache Enthusiasts.

**ApacheCon Europe 2000** is the only Apache Conference and Expo coming
to Europe and the only event to be fully supported by the
[[]Apache Software Foundation](http://www.apache.org/).
Apache founders and leading contributors will design the technical program
which will have a specific European focus. Topics to be covered include
(but are not limited to):

Securing Apache on Windows
Securing Apache on Unix

Security and eCommerce
Java

Performance
Perl

PHP
XML

**ApacheCon Europe 2000!** is an ideal opportunity for you to capitalize
on the Open Source revolution. Meet 1,000 European:

- Open source software developers

- Apache software developers

- Web site administrators

- Technical managers responsible for running Web sites

### A World Class Exhibition Facility Awaits You

Collect leads, conduct demonstrations or have one-on-one discussions
with attendees on a bustling exhibit floor. Take advantage of 12&frac12;
hours of exhibition time over two action-packed days. The Olympia
Conference Centre offers state-of-the-art facilities and easy
accessibility.

### Reasons to Exhibit:

- **Take a Lead** — in the growing Apache base in Europe
by taking a prominent position on the show floor.

- **Great date and location**. Located in London. England - it
will attract attendees from the UK and Europe. Leads from the event
can easily be converted into first quarter sales.

- **Exhibitor packages are available to fit every budget** —
from simple 3sqm booths to large-scale properties coupled with exclusive
keynote opportunities.

- **Be part of a targeted show** where each attendee is a valuable
prospect. Every demo matters!

- **Benefit from a massive advertising campaign.** Be included
in promotional materials being mailed to thousands of qualified prospects
throughout Europe. You'll benefit from our extensive on-line campaign
as well as be listed in advertisements scheduled to appear in major
industry publications.

- **Team up with the Apache Software Foundation** — Meet and
mingle with the "movers and shakers" of the Apache movement.
Network your company and product with leading experts, sought-after
analysts and press and industry influencers.

